# RB BrewBook - Current Sprint Context

## Sprint
Sprint 0 - Project Bootstrap

## Objective
Establish the technical foundation of the application. No business features should be implemented beyond authentication and project setup.

## In Scope

### Infrastructure
- Create the Next.js 15 application
- Configure App Router
- Configure TypeScript
- Configure Tailwind CSS
- Install and configure shadcn/ui
- Configure Supabase client
- Prepare Vercel deployment
- Configure environment variables

### Authentication (UC-001)
- HU-001.1 Login with Google
- HU-001.2 Create user automatically
- HU-001.3 Create default workspace
- HU-001.4 Keep session active
- HU-001.5 Handle authentication errors
- HU-001.6 Never store Google credentials
- HU-001.7 Redirect authenticated users to Dashboard

### Logout (UC-002)
- HU-002.1 Logout
- HU-002.2 Invalidate active session
- HU-002.3 Clear local session data
- HU-002.4 Redirect to Login

## Out of Scope

Do NOT implement:
- Recipe management
- Brewing logs
- Inventory
- Fermentation tracking
- Notifications
- Reports
- Multi-user collaboration
- Payments
- Mobile application

## Definition of Done

A task is complete only if:
- The project builds successfully.
- TypeScript has no errors.
- ESLint passes.
- No secrets are committed.
- Existing architecture is respected.
- Changes are limited to the requested scope.

## Working Agreement

For every request:
1. Read project.mdc first.
2. Explain the implementation plan.
3. Keep changes as small as possible.
4. Do not refactor unrelated code.
5. Wait for approval before major structural changes.
